  <language>en_US</language>
  <keyword>friedman</keyword>
  <short_description>Friedman test for blocked data.</short_description>
  <syntax>
    <syntax_item>p = friedman(X)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>p = friedman(X, reps)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>p = friedman(X, reps, displayopt)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>[p, tbl, stats] = friedman(...)</syntax_item>
  </syntax>
  <description>
    <p><b>friedman</b> performs a nonparametric test for column treatment effects in blocked data. Rows are blocks and columns are treatments.</p>
    <p>When <b>reps</b> is greater than one, each block occupies <b>reps</b> consecutive rows. <b>displayopt</b> can be <b>'on'</b> or <b>'off'</b>.</p>
  </description>
  <examples>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description />
      <example_item_data runnable="cli"><![CDATA[X = [9 7 6; 8 6 5; 7 8 6; 10 9 7; 9 10 8];
[p, tbl, stats] = friedman(X, 'off')]]></example_item_data>
    </example_item>
  </examples>
